# Before Sleep Adhkar
@id before-sleep-adhkar
@version 1
@author santarl
@desc The remembrance of the Sunnah before sleep, for protection through the night.
@desc Ordered from the most authentic. Swipe up or down for the meaning, the transliteration, then the grading, reward and source of each slide.
@desc Arabic follows Hisn al-Muslim; Quranic text is the Tanzil Uthmani text (tanzil.net), unmodified. Translation and transliteration are original.

---1
# Ayat al-Kursi
ٱللَّهُ لَآ إِلَٰهَ إِلَّا هُوَ ٱلْحَىُّ ٱلْقَيُّومُ ۚ | Allah: there is no god but Him, the Ever-Living, the Self-Sustaining. | Allahu la ilaha illa huwal-hayyul-qayyum, | Status: Quran (2:255). Sahih al-Bukhari 2311 / 5010 (Abu Hurayrah). The Prophet ﷺ said of the one who taught it: "He told you the truth although he is a liar." The words taught: "When you go to your bed, recite Ayat al-Kursi … for there will continue to be a guardian over you from Allah, and no devil will come near you until morning."
لَا تَأْخُذُهُۥ سِنَةٌۭ وَلَا نَوْمٌۭ ۚ | Neither drowsiness nor sleep overtakes Him. | la ta'khudhuhu sinatun wa la nawm,
لَّهُۥ مَا فِى ٱلسَّمَٰوَٰتِ وَمَا فِى ٱلْأَرْضِ ۗ | To Him belongs whatever is in the heavens and whatever is on the earth. | lahu ma fis-samawati wa ma fil-ard,
مَن ذَا ٱلَّذِى يَشْفَعُ عِندَهُۥٓ إِلَّا بِإِذْنِهِۦ ۚ | Who is there that can intercede with Him except by His permission? | man dhal-ladhi yashfa'u indahu illa bi'idhnih,
يَعْلَمُ مَا بَيْنَ أَيْدِيهِمْ وَمَا خَلْفَهُمْ ۖ | He knows what is before them and what is behind them, | ya'lamu ma bayna aydihim wa ma khalfahum,
وَلَا يُحِيطُونَ بِشَىْءٍۢ مِّنْ عِلْمِهِۦٓ إِلَّا بِمَا شَآءَ ۚ | and they encompass nothing of His knowledge except what He wills. | wa la yuhituna bishay'in min ilmihi illa bima sha',
وَسِعَ كُرْسِيُّهُ ٱلسَّمَٰوَٰتِ وَٱلْأَرْضَ ۖ | His Throne extends over the heavens and the earth, | wasi'a kursiyyuhus-samawati wal-ard,
وَلَا يَـُٔودُهُۥ حِفْظُهُمَا ۚ | and guarding them does not weigh on Him. | wa la ya'uduhu hifzuhuma,
وَهُوَ ٱلْعَلِىُّ ٱلْعَظِيمُ | He is the Most High, the Most Great. | wa huwal-aliyyul-azim.
---1
# Last two verses of al-Baqarah
ءَامَنَ ٱلرَّسُولُ بِمَآ أُنزِلَ إِلَيْهِ مِن رَّبِّهِۦ وَٱلْمُؤْمِنُونَ ۚ | The Messenger believes in what has been sent down to him from his Lord, and so do the believers. | Amanar-rasulu bima unzila ilayhi mir-rabbihi wal-mu'minun. | Status: Quran (2:285-286). Sahih al-Bukhari 5009; Sahih Muslim 808. Abu Mas'ud al-Ansari reported that the Prophet ﷺ said: "Whoever recites the two verses at the end of Surat al-Baqarah at night, they will suffice him."
كُلٌّ ءَامَنَ بِٱللَّهِ وَمَلَٰٓئِكَتِهِۦ وَكُتُبِهِۦ وَرُسُلِهِۦ | Each one believes in Allah, His angels, His books and His messengers. | Kullun amana billahi wa mala'ikatihi wa kutubihi wa rusulih.
لَا نُفَرِّقُ بَيْنَ أَحَدٍۢ مِّن رُّسُلِهِۦ ۚ | We make no distinction between any of His messengers. | La nufarriqu bayna ahadim-mir-rusulih.
وَقَالُوا۟ سَمِعْنَا وَأَطَعْنَا ۖ | And they say: We hear and we obey. | Wa qalu sami'na wa ata'na.
غُفْرَانَكَ رَبَّنَا وَإِلَيْكَ ٱلْمَصِيرُ | Your forgiveness, our Lord, and to You is the return. | Ghufranaka rabbana wa ilaykal-masir.
لَا يُكَلِّفُ ٱللَّهُ نَفْسًا إِلَّا وُسْعَهَا ۚ | Allah does not burden a soul beyond what it can bear. | La yukallifullahu nafsan illa wus'aha.
لَهَا مَا كَسَبَتْ وَعَلَيْهَا مَا ٱكْتَسَبَتْ ۗ | It gets what it has earned, and is charged with what it has committed. | Laha ma kasabat wa alayha maktasabat.
رَبَّنَا لَا تُؤَاخِذْنَآ إِن نَّسِينَآ أَوْ أَخْطَأْنَا ۚ | Our Lord, do not take us to account if we forget or make a mistake. | Rabbana la tu'akhidhna in nasina aw akhta'na.
رَبَّنَا وَلَا تَحْمِلْ عَلَيْنَآ إِصْرًۭا كَمَا حَمَلْتَهُۥ عَلَى ٱلَّذِينَ مِن قَبْلِنَا ۚ | Our Lord, do not lay on us a burden like that which You laid on those before us. | Rabbana wa la tahmil alayna isran kama hamaltahu alal-ladhina min qablina.
رَبَّنَا وَلَا تُحَمِّلْنَا مَا لَا طَاقَةَ لَنَا بِهِۦ ۖ | Our Lord, do not burden us with what we have no strength to bear. | Rabbana wa la tuhammilna ma la taqata lana bih.
وَٱعْفُ عَنَّا وَٱغْفِرْ لَنَا وَٱرْحَمْنَآ ۚ | Pardon us, forgive us and have mercy on us. | Wa'fu anna waghfir lana warhamna.
أَنتَ مَوْلَىٰنَا فَٱنصُرْنَا عَلَى ٱلْقَوْمِ ٱلْكَٰفِرِينَ | You are our Protector, so help us against the disbelieving people. | Anta mawlana fansurna alal-qawmil-kafirin.
---1
# Surat al-Ikhlas
بِسْمِ ٱللَّهِ ٱلرَّحْمَٰنِ ٱلرَّحِيمِ | In the name of Allah, the Most Gracious, the Most Merciful. | Bismillahir-rahmanir-rahim | Status: Quran (112). Sahih al-Bukhari 5017; Sahih Muslim 2192 (Aishah). She reported that every night when the Prophet ﷺ went to his bed, he would cup his hands together, blow into them, and recite the Mu'awwidhat (al-Ikhlas, al-Falaq, an-Nas), then wipe over as much of his body as he could with his hands, starting with his head and face and the front of his body. He would do that three times.
قُلْ هُوَ ٱللَّهُ أَحَدٌ | Say: He is Allah, the One. | Qul huwallahu ahad.
ٱللَّهُ ٱلصَّمَدُ | Allah, the Eternal Refuge. | Allahus-samad.
لَمْ يَلِدْ وَلَمْ يُولَدْ | He has not begotten, nor was He begotten, | Lam yalid wa lam yulad.
وَلَمْ يَكُن لَّهُۥ كُفُوًا أَحَدٌۢ | and there is none equal to Him. | Wa lam yakun lahu kufuwan ahad.
---1
# Surat al-Falaq
بِسْمِ ٱللَّهِ ٱلرَّحْمَٰنِ ٱلرَّحِيمِ | In the name of Allah, the Most Gracious, the Most Merciful. | Bismillahir-rahmanir-rahim | Status: Quran (113). Part of the three Mu'awwidhat; see the source on Surat al-Ikhlas (Sahih al-Bukhari 5017; Sahih Muslim 2192).
قُلْ أَعُوذُ بِرَبِّ ٱلْفَلَقِ | Say: I seek refuge in the Lord of daybreak, | Qul a'udhu birabbil-falaq,
مِن شَرِّ مَا خَلَقَ | from the evil of what He has created, | min sharri ma khalaq,
وَمِن شَرِّ غَاسِقٍ إِذَا وَقَبَ | from the evil of the darkness when it settles, | wa min sharri ghasiqin idha waqab,
وَمِن شَرِّ ٱلنَّفَّٰثَٰتِ فِى ٱلْعُقَدِ | from the evil of those who blow on knots, | wa min sharrin-naffathati fil-'uqad,
وَمِن شَرِّ حَاسِدٍ إِذَا حَسَدَ | and from the evil of an envier when he envies. | wa min sharri hasidin idha hasad.
---1
# Surat an-Nas
بِسْمِ ٱللَّهِ ٱلرَّحْمَٰنِ ٱلرَّحِيمِ | In the name of Allah, the Most Gracious, the Most Merciful. | Bismillahir-rahmanir-rahim | Status: Quran (114). Part of the three Mu'awwidhat; see the source on Surat al-Ikhlas (Sahih al-Bukhari 5017; Sahih Muslim 2192).
قُلْ أَعُوذُ بِرَبِّ ٱلنَّاسِ | Say: I seek refuge in the Lord of mankind, | Qul a'udhu birabbin-nas,
مَلِكِ ٱلنَّاسِ | the King of mankind, | malikin-nas,
إِلَٰهِ ٱلنَّاسِ | the God of mankind, | ilahin-nas,
مِن شَرِّ ٱلْوَسْوَاسِ ٱلْخَنَّاسِ | from the evil of the whisperer who slinks away, | min sharril-waswasil-khannas,
ٱلَّذِى يُوَسْوِسُ فِى صُدُورِ ٱلنَّاسِ | who whispers in the hearts of mankind, | alladhi yuwaswisu fi sudurin-nas,
مِنَ ٱلْجِنَّةِ وَٱلنَّاسِ | from among the jinn and mankind. | minal-jinnati wan-nas.
---1
# After the three Quls
[10]Aishah reported that the Prophet ﷺ would cup his hands, blow into them after reciting the three surahs, then wipe over as much of his body as he could, beginning with the head and face and the front of his body, and that he would do so three times. (Sahih al-Bukhari 5017; Sahih Muslim 2192)
---33
# Subhanallah
سُبْحَانَ ٱللَّهِ | Glory be to Allah. | Subhanallah. | Status: Sahih al-Bukhari 5361 / 6318 (Ali). Fatimah came to the Prophet ﷺ asking for a servant. He said: "Shall I not tell you of something better for you than a servant? When you go to your beds, glorify Allah (say Subhanallah) thirty-three times, praise Him (say Alhamdulillah) thirty-three times, and magnify Him (say Allahu Akbar) thirty-four times."
---33
# Alhamdulillah
ٱلْحَمْدُ لِلَّهِ | All praise is for Allah. | Alhamdulillah. | Status: Sahih al-Bukhari 5361 / 6318. Part of the same report to Fatimah and Ali (see previous slide).
---34
# Allahu Akbar
ٱللَّهُ أَكْبَرُ | Allah is the Greatest. | Allahu akbar. | Status: Sahih al-Bukhari 5361 / 6318. Completes the hundred taught before sleep (33 + 33 + 34).
---1
# In Your name I die and live
بِٱسْمِكَ ٱللَّهُمَّ أَمُوتُ وَأَحْيَا | In Your name, O Allah, I die and I live. | Bismika Allahumma amutu wa ahya. | Status: Sahih al-Bukhari 6314 / 6324 (Hudhayfah). "Whenever the Prophet ﷺ lay down for sleep at night, he would place his (right) hand under his (right) cheek and say: 'Bismika Allahumma amutu wa ahya.'"
---1
# In Your name, my Lord, I lay down my side
بِٱسْمِكَ رَبِّى وَضَعْتُ جَنْبِى وَبِكَ أَرْفَعُهُۥ ۖ إِنْ أَمْسَكْتَ نَفْسِى فَٱرْحَمْهَا ۖ وَإِنْ أَرْسَلْتَهَا فَٱحْفَظْهَا بِمَا تَحْفَظُ بِهِۦ عِبَادَكَ ٱلصَّٰلِحِينَ | In Your name, my Lord, I lay down my side, and by You I raise it. If You take my soul, have mercy on it; if You send it back, protect it as You protect Your righteous servants. | Bismika rabbi wada'tu janbi, wa bika arfa'uh. In amsakta nafsi farhamha, wa in arsaltaha fahfazha bima tahfazu bihi ibadakas-salihin. | Status: Sahih al-Bukhari 7393; Sahih Muslim 2714 (Abu Hurayrah / others). When the Prophet ﷺ wanted to lie down he would say this.
---1
# O Allah, Knower of the unseen
أَللَّهُمَّ عَٰلِمَ ٱلْغَيْبِ وَٱلشَّهَٰدَةِ فَاطِرَ ٱلسَّمَٰوَٰتِ وَٱلْأَرْضِ رَبَّ كُلِّ شَىْءٍ وَمَلِيكَهُۥ أَشْهَدُ أَن لَّآ إِلَٰهَ إِلَّآ أَنتَ أَعُوذُ بِكَ مِن شَرِّ نَفْسِى وَمِن شَرِّ ٱلشَّيْطَٰنِ وَشِرْكِهِۦ وَأَنْ أَقْتَرِفَ عَلَىٰ نَفْسِى سُوٓءًا أَوْ أَجُرَّهُۥٓ إِلَىٰ مُسْلِمٍ | O Allah, Knower of the unseen and the seen, Creator of the heavens and the earth, Lord of everything and its Master, I bear witness that there is no god but You. I seek refuge in You from the evil of my soul, from the evil of Satan and his partnership, and from bringing evil upon myself or harming any Muslim. | Allahumma alimal-ghaybi wash-shahadah, fatiras-samawati wal-ard, rabba kulli shay'in wa malikah, ashhadu an la ilaha illa ant. A'udhu bika min sharri nafsi, wa min sharrish-shaytani wa shirkih, wa an aqtarifa ala nafsi su'an aw ajurrahu ila muslim. | Status: Sahih (Abu Dawud 5067; at-Tirmidhi 3392; al-Albani). Abu Bakr asked the Prophet ﷺ for words to say in the morning, evening and when he took to his bed; he taught him this.
---1
# Lord of the seven heavens
أَللَّهُمَّ رَبَّ ٱلسَّمَٰوَٰتِ ٱلسَّبْعِ وَرَبَّ ٱلْعَرْشِ ٱلْعَظِيمِ رَبَّنَا وَرَبَّ كُلِّ شَىْءٍ فَالِقَ ٱلْحَبِّ وَٱلنَّوَىٰ وَمُنزِلَ ٱلتَّوْرَىٰةِ وَٱلْإِنجِيلِ وَٱلْفُرْقَانِ أَعُوذُ بِكَ مِن شَرِّ كُلِّ شَىْءٍ أَنتَ ءَاخِذٌۢ بِنَاصِيَتِهِۦ أَللَّهُمَّ أَنتَ ٱلْأَوَّلُ فَلَيْسَ قَبْلَكَ شَىْءٌ وَأَنتَ ٱلْءَاخِرُ فَلَيْسَ بَعْدَكَ شَىْءٌ وَأَنتَ ٱلظَّٰهِرُ فَلَيْسَ فَوْقَكَ شَىْءٌ وَأَنتَ ٱلْبَاطِنُ فَلَيْسَ دُونَكَ شَىْءٌ ٱقْضِ عَنَّا ٱلدَّيْنَ وَأَغْنِنَا مِنَ ٱلْفَقْرِ | O Allah, Lord of the seven heavens and Lord of the Mighty Throne, our Lord and the Lord of everything, Splitter of the grain and the date-stone, Revealer of the Torah, the Gospel and the Criterion, I seek refuge in You from the evil of everything You seize by the forelock. O Allah, You are the First and nothing is before You; You are the Last and nothing is after You; You are the Most High and nothing is above You; You are the Most Near and nothing is nearer than You. Settle our debt for us and enrich us against poverty. | Allahumma rabbas-samawatis-sab'i wa rabbal-arshil-azim, rabbana wa rabba kulli shay', faliqal-habbi wan-nawa, wa munzilat-tawrati wal-injili wal-furqan. A'udhu bika min sharri kulli shay'in anta akhidhun binasiyatih. Allahumma antal-awwalu fa laysa qablaka shay', wa antal-akhiru fa laysa ba'daka shay', wa antaz-zahiru fa laysa fawqaka shay', wa antal-batinu fa laysa dunaka shay'. Iqdi annad-dayn wa aghnina minal-faqr. | Status: Sahih Muslim 2713 (Abu Hurayrah). The Prophet ﷺ would say this when he went to bed.
---1
# I submit myself to You
أَللَّهُمَّ أَسْلَمْتُ نَفْسِى إِلَيْكَ وَفَوَّضْتُ أَمْرِى إِلَيْكَ وَوَجَّهْتُ وَجْهِى إِلَيْكَ وَأَلْجَأْتُ ظَهْرِى إِلَيْكَ رَغْبَةً وَرَهْبَةً إِلَيْكَ لَا مَلْجَأَ وَلَا مَنْجَا مِنْكَ إِلَّا إِلَيْكَ ءَامَنْتُ بِكِتَٰبِكَ ٱلَّذِىٓ أَنزَلْتَ وَبِنَبِيِّكَ ٱلَّذِىٓ أَرْسَلْتَ | O Allah, I submit myself to You, entrust my affairs to You, turn my face to You, and lay myself down depending upon You, hoping in You and fearing You. There is no refuge and no escape from You except to You. I believe in Your Book which You revealed and in Your Prophet whom You sent. | Allahumma aslamtu nafsi ilayk, wa fawwadtu amri ilayk, wa wajjahtu wajhi ilayk, wa alja'tu zahri ilayk, raghbatan wa rahbatan ilayk, la malja'a wa la manja minka illa ilayk. Amantu bikitabikal-ladhi anzalt, wa binabiyyikal-ladhi arsalt. | Status: Sahih al-Bukhari 247 / 6311; Sahih Muslim 2710 (al-Bara' ibn Azib). The Prophet ﷺ said: "When you go to bed, perform ablution as you do for prayer, then lie down on your right side and say [this]. … If you die that night, you will die upon the fitrah (natural monotheism)." He also said: "Make them the last words you say."
